\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The verifier does two jobs. Reading left to right along the trajectory, it mines the case: the text typed at step $t$ appears in the OCR of screen 1 and not on screen $t$. Applied to every earlier screen instead of stopping at the first hit, the same test labels all $t$ candidates. Those labels train two instantiations that differ in how the history reaches the model, and therefore in how many decisions one label set yields.}}{3}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:method}{{1}{3}{The verifier does two jobs. Reading left to right along the trajectory, it mines the case: the text typed at step $t$ appears in the OCR of screen 1 and not on screen $t$. Applied to every earlier screen instead of stopping at the first hit, the same test labels all $t$ candidates. Those labels train two instantiations that differ in how the history reaches the model, and therefore in how many decisions one label set yields}{figure.caption.7}{}}
